Find the magnitude, then divide each component by it.
$\begin{aligned}|\underset{\sim}{a}|&=\sqrt{(-8)^2+(-6)^2}\\&=10\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}\hat{\underset{\sim}{a}}&=\frac{\underset{\sim}{a}}{|\underset{\sim}{a}|}\\&=\frac{1}{10}(-8\mathbf{i}-6\mathbf{j})\\&=-\frac45\mathbf{i}-\frac35\mathbf{j}\end{aligned}$
The unit vector has the same direction and one tenth of the original length.
